# Hand-authored leaf stamps: one folder per source, each holding a diffuse
# (sRGB, alpha carries the cutout), an arm and a 16-bit disp map. One leaf per
# stamp, pivot at bottom-middle and tip at top-middle, which is what lets the
# forge arrange them into a cluster without per-source metadata. No normal map —
# tree-forge derives it after rotation. See ../../../../docs/tree-forge.md.
#
# Large binaries, kept out of git the way /assets/ is. With no source here the
# forge generates its leaves instead, so a fresh clone still builds. This rule
# keeps the file itself tracked so the folder survives that clone.
*
!.gitignore
